# Environment for an ANONYMOUS Resume Matcher instance.
# Copy to resume-matcher.anon.env (git-ignored) on the VPS.
#
# Deliberately no LLM_API_KEY: an anonymous visitor must not be able to spend your model
# budget. The app handles a missing key by pointing at its own Settings page, where the
# visitor pastes their own. If you would rather fund a shared demo key, add it here and
# accept that any visitor can spend it — the app's only cap is global per instance.

# MANDATORY since the 2026-09 builds: the app aborts startup on an empty TENANT_MODE
# rather than guess who may see whose resumes.
#
# `header` is the right value behind this gateway, not `single`. The broker sends
# X-Apps-Tenant / X-Apps-Role on every request, and a `single` instance treats any request
# carrying them as a bypass attempt and answers 404 — the app boots, and then every call
# fails except /api/v1/health, which is exempt.
#
# GATEWAY_SECRET is what makes those headers trustworthy: without it a client could send
# X-Apps-Role: admin itself. The broker reads it out of *this* file and sends it back as
# X-Apps-Proxy-Secret, so the two sides cannot drift — there is one value, in one place.
# Generate per instance with `openssl rand -hex 32`; it must be ASCII.
TENANT_MODE=header
GATEWAY_SECRET=replace-me-openssl-rand-hex-32

LLM_PROVIDER=
LLM_MODEL=
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
